# Settings of the ASP node-agent (a systemd EnvironmentFile: KEY=value, one per line, no
# quotes). Mode 0600. The unit already sets the ones every node needs (KVM, the
# egress proxy, mTLS); these are the ones that differ between nodes. The flags and
# variables are listed by `asp-node-agent -h`, and `sudo asp doctor` checks the host.
#
# The control plane this node joins, and the certificate that signed its TLS:
#ASP_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://cp.example.corp:8443
#ASP_CONTROL_PLANE_CA=/etc/asp/cp-ca.pem
#
# How the control plane reaches this node (mutual TLS):
#ASP_AGENT_TLS_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:9443
#ASP_ENDPOINT=https://node1.example.corp:9443
#
# First start only: enroll, then remove both lines once the journal says "enrolled"
# (the token must not stay in this file). Get a token on the control plane with
# `asp node enroll-token --node-id node1`.
#ASP_ENROLL=1
#ASP_NODE_ENROLL_TOKEN=
#
# The guest kernel and image every sandbox boots (these are the defaults):
#ASP_GUEST_KERNEL=/opt/sandbox/vmlinux
#ASP_GUEST_ROOTFS=/opt/sandbox/rootfs.img
